A||||3||fropuff||Trunk carpet removal?||||4||
Z||000000||fropuff||08-17-2000||01:22 PM||||Hey, I was wondering how to remove the trunk carpet on my '86 GT.  I want to do this to make it easier to run the wire for DXR_DAD's back-up light mod.  How can I do this?  Thanks.||||reg||4
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-17-2000||01:28 PM||||there are 2.25" grey plastic "buttons" in the trunk.. grab 2 sides of them and pull really quick. they'll pop out of their holes.. once those are out i think theres 4 or 5.. 3 on the front (near the engine) and 2 in the tail light area. then pull the light out of its place in the center of the carpet.. unplug the light and lift the carpet up... <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/emptytrunk.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||HugGRRRFiero||08-17-2000||01:41 PM||||  If you don't want to break those grey tree clip/washer thingys, then try using a claw hammer or something similar to grab around the tree and not break it.  After you get those out, just start with a corner and pull, it should come right out.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-19-2000||05:05 PM||||Even with a tool they are likely to break as not.||||reg||1
